{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/835084-doing-a-custom-cofd-missing-one-key-element","id":835084,"title":"Doing a Custom CofD, Missing One Key Element","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-22T08:50:10-08:00","id":835084,"title":"Doing a Custom CofD, Missing One Key Element","content":"I'm more familar with WoD than CoD (though I do own books from both systems, and have followed them for years), so I'm not entirely sure if what I'm doing is either possible, or already kinda-sorta handled elsewhere. Hence this topic.<br /> <br /> So let me begin. I've had a custom Urban Fantasy setting in my head for a while now, but I've never seen a system that supports fully what I want to do (closest I've ever seen if the old Everlasting RPG, which I don't own). Having gone over some of the new 2nd edition materials, i'm beginning to see how I can mold CofD into what I need, with some work. Important thing to undestand is that I'm using almost none of the CofD lore, as it's my own setting.<br /> <br /> Here's what I've got:<br /> <br /> Vampires, covered by Requiem. Replacing Clans with Subspecies (pun intended), based off different cultural styles of vampires. Yeah, I know the Clans are supposed to reflect that, but its all too cookie-cutter for me. I want to be more like the Dresden Files where the vampire types have noticeable differences, not just &quot;carbon copies with one differing weakness and a different set of default starting powers).<br /> <br /> Werewolves: this one is following more of the CofD design, as I like the Forsaken story, and my own is somewhat similar. The main difference is that the Pure represent purebred werewolves who interbreed amongst their own kind, versus the Mongrels, who are bitten and cursed. With the Mongrels being a kind of underclass, similar to the Pureblood/Turned class divide in the Blade movies. The Pure have lineages, the Mongrels form packs.<br /> <br /> Mages: ditching the whole Atlantean/Exarch thing (interesting idea but doesn't fit my setting). Replacing the group with Traditions (not like Ascension!) that define a magickal style (Hermetic, Shamanistic, Voudoun, Ancestral, Blood, etc). Still use the base arcana and rotes, but striking a balance between Awakening's rigidity and Ascension's free-form system.<br /> <br /> Hunter: completely unchanged aside from the fact that I'll be using different conspiracies and groups.<br /> <br /> Changeling: I'm not familiar with it in CofD (sacrilege, I know), so i don't know how I want to incorporate it yet.<br /> <br /> Promethean &amp; Geist: Unused<br /> <br /> Mummy: Same deal as Changeling, but from what I've skimmed, I don't think I'll be tweaking much beyond factions there either.<br /> <br /> Demons/Angels: For this, I'm using the Demon Translation guide to bring Fallen in to replace Descent. Sorry, the gnostic technoangels just dont' fit what I have in mind. For a &quot;toolbox&quot; system, dropping a major spat so intimately tied to a single campaign, and such a unique one at that, was very disappointing for me. WoD's Fallen is near perfect for my purposes, aside from the fact that I want to make Angelic counterparts of the Demon groups for NPCs.<br /> <br /> So here's what I want that I can't find an equivalent there in. I want Demigods, mortal descendants of the old gods. They should be the closest thing this world gets to &quot;superheroes&quot; and even that isn't realy accurate. They're mostly human, except when they trigger, they get powers related to their otherworldly parent's pantheon. Say a descendant of Thor would have the ability to control weather in a limited area. Sounds awesome, and kinda not &quot;WoD-like&quot; except for two problems. First, their powers are fueled by either adoration or fear. So hence the save people/terrorize thing, very similar to Beat the Primordial. The other problem is, a quick route to more power is to kill and consume the essence of another Demigod, so the more attention you attract, the bigger target you paint on yourself. Or will you become a predator of your own kind, instead. Kind of a dark nudge and wink at how superheroes and villains always seem more focused on fighting each other than doing anything proactive to better the world.<br /> <br /> Problem is, aside from Beast having a mechanical weakness I can rip off, I don't know any other Storyteller game that has anything even CLOSE to the power system I want to use. I'm basically looking for recommendations of fan splats or sourcebook that I don't own, that might point me in the right direction, as this is basically building a new spin-off core game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:03:10-08:00","id":835091,"title":"","content":"Changeling might actually do something like what you want (with tweaking, of course). Changelings look mortal up until they start doing magic; they have very codified power sets that vary greatly from each other; they fuel their powers from collecting emotions. Obviously their flavor would change greatly, but it hits all your bases except for the consuming-others mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:34:43-08:00","id":835108,"title":"","content":"Crap, this was supposed to go in the base Chronicles of Darkness forum! Um, can a mod move this, or should I just delete my OP and repost it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:35:25-08:00","id":835109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/835084-doing-a-custom-cofd-missing-one-key-element?p=835091#post835091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling might actually do something like what you want (with tweaking, of course). Changelings look mortal up until they start doing magic; they have very codified power sets that vary greatly from each other; they fuel their powers from collecting emotions. Obviously their flavor would change greatly, but it hits all your bases except for the consuming-others mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, i'll go bug a friend of mine for his copy of the 1st Ed book and give it a once over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T19:30:51-08:00","id":835521,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at Scion? It's a different setting/system, but it's pretty much all about the exact thing you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T20:41:35-08:00","id":835560,"title":"","content":"Scion? I'm not familiar with it, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T04:32:43-08:00","id":835675,"title":"","content":"I had an idea a while back that you could model Scions in CoD using the spirit-claimed rules with a bit of tweaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T19:11:44-08:00","id":836153,"title":"","content":"It's a game by White Wolf that's literally all about playing the children of classical mythological deities in a modern setting. There's a forum all about it on this very website! It's going to get a second edition sometime in the possibly-near future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T21:58:58-08:00","id":836240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/835084-doing-a-custom-cofd-missing-one-key-element?p=836153#post836153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a game by White Wolf that's literally all about playing the children of classical mythological deities in a modern setting. There's a forum all about it on this very website! It's going to get a second edition sometime in the possibly-near future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I've never heard of it. Or have it? Did it used to be owned by TSR before they went under? And does it use something resembling the Storyteller system, perchance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T00:36:51-08:00","id":836285,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty similar system in 1st. I think the second edition is shaking things up a bit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:46:18-08:00","id":836764,"title":"","content":"Nope, it was a White Wolf original. More similar to Aberrant than anything else, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T01:28:57-08:00","id":836918,"title":"","content":"Ok, I played Scion once as a one-off a while back, so my memory is a little fuzzy, but it's in the same basic ball park as storyteller. Roll d10s, count successes, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.j